    "title": "**SPOILERS** - AEW Collision Results For February 7, 2026 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Anthony Mango ,\n1 hours ago\nThis Saturday’s edition of AEW Collision (airing February 7, 2026) was taped in advance after AEW Dynamite on February 4th at the Pearl Theater in Las Vegas.\nAccording to various reports and sources (namely PWI ), the following SPOILERS took place during these tapings.\nREAD MORE: Brody King Squashes MJF On AEW Dynamite, Ricochet Cheats To Win, Drilla Moloney Injured\nREAD MORE: 5 Huge AEW Grand Slam: Australia Matches Set, Updated AEW Collision Lineup (2/7/26)\nObviously, if you don’t want to know who wins the matches and what else happens before it airs, don’t read what’s below.\nHere are your results for AEW Collision this week:\nThe Young Bucks defeated GOA by pinfall. Kris Statlander revealed her match with Thekla for the title on next week’s Dynamite will be a strap match. She was then attacked by The Triangle of Madness. Tommaso Ciampa defeated Roderick Strong and Claudio Castagnoli to retain the AEW TNT Championship by pinfall. Afterward, Kyle Fletcher challenged Ciampa to a match on Dynamite. Kevin Knight defeated Scorpio Sky by pinfall. Mina Shirakawa defeated Viva Van by submission. TBD What do you think about these spoilers? Drop a comment below!",
    "summary": "This Saturday’s edition of AEW Collision (airing February 7, 2026) was taped in advance after AEW Dynamite on February 4th at the Pearl Theater in Las Vegas. READ MORE: Brody King Squashes MJF On AEW Dynamite, Ricochet Cheats To Win, Drilla Moloney Injured READ MORE: 5 Huge AEW Grand Slam: Australia Matches Set, Updated AEW Collision Lineup (2/7/26) Obviously, if you don’t want to know who wins the matches and what else happens before it airs, don’t read what’s below. Here are your results for AEW Collision this week: The Young Bucks defeated GOA by pinfall.",
